{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>These are the appointed times of HaShem.</b> After he spoke of the Sabbath, whose appointed time is already fixed — as the Sages, of blessed memory, stated (Pesaḥim, chapter 4): שַׁבָּת הִיא דְּקַבְעָה אַנַּפְשַׁהּ — he began with the matter of the appointed times whose timing is set through the court's declaration, as it says in the received tradition (Rosh HaShanah 25a): אַתֶּם אֲפִילוּ שׁוֹגְגִין, אַתֶּם אֲפִילוּ מְזִידִין, אַתֶּם אֲפִילוּ מוּטְעִין."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Sforno cites Pesaḥim chapter 4; the Aramaic citation שַׁבָּת הִיא דְּקַבְעָה אַנַּפְשַׁהּ ('the Sabbath fixed itself') appears in Pesaḥim 117a. The Rosh HaShanah citation is from 25a, normalized from the leaf mark כ׳ה."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:28.672700816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}